diff --git a/.omx/research/ddm_pm2_instrument_laws_as_structural_gates_20260909.md b/.omx/research/ddm_pm2_instrument_laws_as_structural_gates_20260909.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..c3e1f46bd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.omx/research/ddm_pm2_instrument_laws_as_structural_gates_20260909.md
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# ddm_pm2 — instrument laws as structural gates
+
+Tokens: `[no-triality] [p0-ledger-ok]`. Apparatus only; `research_only=true`, `score_claim=false`.
+# FORMALIZATION_PENDING: instrument custody and source-order enforcement, no newly measured scoring law
+
+The exact frontier did not move. Four gate surfaces are implemented and fixture-tested. Ledger and pointer-binding preflights are STRICT; charter screening remains warn-only because its live declaration count is nonzero. No pose, pricing, training, scorer, or paid dispatch ran. Reading and hashing retained runtime files is a custody check, not a new score.
+
+## Results and scope
+
+All counts below are MEASURED [macOS-CPU static apparatus / scorer-free test fixtures].
+
+| Gate | Observed before | After / enforcement | Incident-shaped evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Pose base | Three current population producers; six current pair producers needed explicit magnitude checks | All nine guarded before base persistence, default ON | 20 mocked wiring tests plus shared helper cases; gross missing-overlay fixture refuses |
+| Encoder belongs to pointer | Stale cl2 encoder and current cmp2 tree read from disk | cmp2 PASS; cl2 typed refusal; five pricing entrypoints guarded, four shell callers inherit jg2 guard | Real tree hashes, no encoding; 57 shared-helper/wiring tests cover custody, waivers, ordering, and pose cases |
+| Ledger before optional dump | 14 call-site findings in 4/698 producers | 0/698, STRICT #414 | 37 tests, including actual rp1 writer with injected NPZ failure and readable retained ledger |
+| Screening declaration | 93/371 charter declaration warnings | 93/371, WARN #416; explicit strict mode supported | 35 tests, including queue refusal and warning before append |
+
+The combined focused/new and existing affected suites pass **263 tests**. Ruff passes every changed Python file. Logs and exact argv: `.omx/research/ddm_pm2_20260909/checks.json`, `check_0.log`, `check_1.log`. These tests do not measure research efficacy or validate a contest candidate. Static counts describe each detector's stated scope, not global absence of the bug class.
+
+## Gate behavior
+
+Pose population checks snapshot the pointer before measurement and read d_pose from its promoted source receipt. The receipt's SHA must match both the mirror and the pointer's own pin; archive, runtime digest, n600 and passed status must agree. Pointer changes during measurement refuse. The measured mean must lie in [1/3,3] of the reference before an NPY or report can be written as base. `--pose-base-differs-because` requires a concrete rationale and yields an explicit waiver receipt. Nonfinite/negative values cannot be excused by that flag.
+
+Pair-level fe1/rw1 measurements use `--base-pose-reference`, a finite nonnegative n600 NPY vector. Both its population mean and the supplied population scalar are checked against the pointer; measured pairs are compared with their matching reference pairs. Comparing an individual hard pair with the population mean would create false alarms. Reference bytes are hashed and read once. Existing archive/carrier identity checks remain: a threefold magnitude test cannot prove the exact render or detect every wrong subset.
+
+The coder gate resolves the pointer's runtime through its promoted receipt and fire manifest, checks its archive and pinned runtime custody, then hashes both source trees with **the same** `tac.candidate_seal.measure_runtime_digest` function. It never equates that digest with Modal's separately named uploaded-tree digest. On the inspected move37 trees, cmp2 is `4ce85e0c68fb72736d1032597da0c3f403345a4ce18f7231cce56746f5f91a9c`; the stale cl2 encoder is `ce20617dc7db4ff46e13f7acc725e44ae2833696160af039ab7da8bf4033dfc3`. Its current pinned Modal digest remains `165df8de74e584e2a5692471f2a7d5b81db1537a232f4ee0ecaf604b5347c27a`. The stale successor-price shell now refuses before compilation. Experimental tc1/sm1/rc3 pricing additionally requires `--coder-differs-because`: hashing the source decoder alone cannot certify a new encoder imported from experiments. Gate receipts are retained alongside pricing metadata; downstream byte-identity controls remain in force.
+
+Gates 1–2 are default ON. **`TAC_INSTRUMENT_GATES=0` is the explicit escape for a process already mid-run.** It preserves legacy calculations and emits a typed invalid bypass receipt. Gates refuse or document explicit exceptions; they never rescale or change measured values. The shell wrappers expose a rationale through `CODER_DIFFERS_BECAUSE`, forwarded as the actual CLI flag. No running scorer or live arm was restarted.
+
+Ledger fixes cover rp1's older rank writer (the mixer had already been cured), nr1/tb2 empty accepted sets, and pc2 incremental price rows. A named in-memory `ledger_rows.append` is not persistence. The bounded AST detector distinguishes optional candidate NPZs from checkpoints which already contain the ledger; unknown aliases/interprocedural mutations remain outside its proof. Same-line waivers must be actual substantive comments, not strings or nearby text.
+
+Screening lint checks the OPTIMAL FORM declaration. A subset SCOPE needs actuator confinement; a global subset screen without a substantive TOY-BRACKET is a verdict-invalid MECHANISM reduction. Planned later n600 confirmation does not silently legalize the screen. Of 371 charters, 93 lack declarations under the detector; this does not establish that 93 mechanisms are invalid. rw1's original charter omits its later subset screen and therefore does not fire; implementation drift is outside this declaration lint. fe1 fires, rp1/bnd1/pm2 do not. Strict-flipping with this nonzero census would violate the charter's flip condition.
+
+## Prediction and falsifier accounting
+
+The stale-coder prediction was confirmed by real retained tree hashes. Ledger prediction 2–6 is met if an instance means a producer (four), exceeded if it means a call site (14). Screening prediction at most three is falsified by 93 declaration findings over 371 charters.
+
+Pose historical evidence is read-back, not fresh measurement: sj1's recorded base 5.7675e-6 versus 5.77e-6 is 0.99957x; its correct pass4 base 5.090165e-6 versus pc2 5.09276404439735e-6 is 0.99949x. The no-overlay base 2.559e-3 is approximately 502.7x the correct base and would refuse. rp1 independently records 5.049765771412152e-6 versus the current 5.05e-6 component (0.999954x). No band falsifier was found in these scoped receipts. This is **not** a verified seven-of-seven move31–37 baseline census and does not justify widening or disabling the band.
+
+Pose source census parsed 698 ddm files with zero syntax errors: ten name-matched base assignments, six current guarded pair producers and four historical distinct-vehicle instruments (bs4y, jg5, qs1, qs5) outside this live-vehicle gate. Three tagged population producers were separately traced. Imposing today's pointer mean on historical vehicles would itself confound the instrument.
+
+## RECALL EVIDENCE
+
+Read the complete charter and common contract, PROGRAM, relevant CLAUDE/AGENTS contracts, operating manual, live main board and actual canonical pointer. The common contract's old frontier paragraph is superseded by the pointer. Searches were content-based across `.omx/research/`, not limited to seed filenames.
+
+- Queries: `pose.base|ledger.*dump|stale.coder|runtime.digest.*definition|screening.law`, plus narrower `ledger.{0,80}(dump|persist)|concatenate\(\[\]\)|ledger loss` and `pair.confined|screening law|global actuator|subset screen|screen.*MECHANISM`.
+- Canonical equations: executed `.venv/bin/python tools/list_canonical_equations.py --json`, 480 rows; retained hash/count and selected identifiers in `equations_recall_summary.json`. No applicable ledger-before-dump or declared subset-screen law was found in the bounded matching queries.
+- Research index/DAG: searched `CANONICAL_RESEARCH_INDEX*` and `sub015_DAG_*` for pose/base/instrument, subset screens and ledger persistence. DAG micro-finisher SCREEN→CONFIRM and g3 rank-correlation evidence reinforce that subset ranking has no verdict authority. The vo1 reopen ledger flags top24 ranking as a naive instrument. This preserved the requirement for an explicit global-screen bracket even when full confirmation is planned.
+- Docs/SPEC/task stores: searched `docs/` specification/design surfaces, canonical task ledger and operator P0 ledger with the same content terms. The scg2 charter and live board identify two digest definitions; source inspection showed scg2 already names both in the current fire manifest. This changed implementation from comparing stored hashes to hashing both trees with the seal definition.
+- Beyond seeds: rxc1's complete checkpoint includes the bit ledger, so it must not be mistaken for an optional dump. Additional fe1 and rw1 pose-base producers joined the fix. rp1's mixer cure already existed but its older rank sibling remained vulnerable. Existing #899 memory guidance supplied the actual-comment waiver and explicit-census precedent; current source/tests supplied the verdict.
+
+Detailed recall, source scope, tests and review notes: `pose_gate.md`, `ledger_review.md`, and the census JSONs under `.omx/research/ddm_pm2_20260909/`.
+
+## Review, integration and custody
+
+Two visible review passes and `review_tracker.py mark-file` marks cover every changed Python file. Root `tests/` is outside the tracker's supported census, so new tests live in `src/tac/tests/`. Review found and fixed: in-memory ledger append falsely certifying persistence; guard proof expiry after mutation; fake waiver strings; unused/dead guard calls; and a same-archive/different-runtime source receipt substitution accepted through a self-consistent mirror. The latter now checks the pointer's pinned receipt SHA and runtime before adopting d_pose. No review override is used.
+
+Catalog claims 414–416 were made through `claim_catalog_number.py`; pose and coder share umbrella #415. The existing file-level quota waiver passes the quota gate; no live protection was retired. New strict calls are wired in `preflight_all`. Four requested runtime/lint surfaces have catalog documentation. The six solver integration hooks are N/A: this apparatus adds no sensitivity, Pareto constraint, byte allocation, deployable candidate, empirical score anchor or competing research hypothesis. Production preflight/CLI/charter consumers are the integration points; no solver efficacy is claimed.
+
+Unrelated dirty state is preserved. The shared queue tool acquired concurrent model-routing edits; `screening_only.patch` contains only pm2's hunks. Serializer uses an explicit patch and post-edit content hashes with no attribution trailer, preserving the shared staged index. Landing status and exact retained bundles are recorded in `LANDING_HANDOFF.json`. Serializer rc17 at `git_apply_cached` is a sandbox Git object write denial, not a patch conflict: the isolated fallback was constructed and `git bundle verify` passes. Code fallback commit `504cbbb0afc22239bf49cab0db11175965f776d1` is retained, **not landed on main**. All 31 intended file hashes match its receipt; concurrent queue-model hunks are excluded. Shared staged paths stayed empty and HEAD did not move. The raw index checksum changed, so byte-for-byte index preservation is not claimed. A stale rp1 checkpoint first produced rc9; the charter explicitly authorizes these refusal-only live-arm edits, so the documented paired-env ownership override was used with isolated patch mode, not a review override.
